# Local scratch: input scenes, run outputs and logs. These are large, are never
# needed at build time, and are exactly what inflates an image built from a
# working tree that has been used.
in/
out/
_e2e*
_nodata*
*.log
*.png
# Scene archives and failing-case captures kept beside the repo while debugging.
# These were 10.5 GB of a build context that is otherwise ~200 MB, and because
# they sit above the Containerfile's `COPY . .` they were also being baked into
# the image. Untracked, so CI never saw them -- only local builds.
demo-data-source/
failing_file/

# 53 MB of spectral libraries that nothing in the repository references -- no
# code, no config, no Containerfile path. They are an archive of the convolved
# delivery libraries kept for provenance, and `COPY . .` was baking them into
# every image and every pull. The libraries the pipeline actually reads are
# under tetracorder/sl1/, which stays.
tetracorder/sl1-archive/

